. * If avg returned 0 switchers, the diagnosis is in the S_g filter.
. * Re-create the Fg / Dg1 / avg_post / Sg variables outside the function so we
. * can `list` them and see why every group fails the switcher test.
. di as text _newline "  ---- Manual replication of S_g logic ----"

  ---- Manual replication of S_g logic ----

. 
. use "`data'", clear

. 
. * Tg_class : last period in the panel for the baseline class.
. *   For continuous treatment, each group is its own class (period-one treatment
. *   is essentially unique per group), so Tg_class = last observed time per g.
. bys `g': egen Tg_class = max(`t')

. 
. * Fg : first period where treatment differs from period-1 value
. gen double d_t1 = `d' if `t' == 1994            // 1994 is first year in favara
(11,493 missing values generated)

. bys `g': egen double Dg1 = max(d_t1)
(19 missing values generated)

. gen byte switched_now = (`d' != Dg1) & !missing(`d') & !missing(Dg1)

. bys `g': egen Fg = min(cond(switched_now, `t', .))
(1,556 missing values generated)

. 
. * avg_post : average treatment over [Fg, Tg_class]
. gen double dpost = `d' if `t' >= Fg & `t' <= Tg_class
(4,919 missing values generated)

. bys `g': egen avg_post = mean(dpost)
(1,556 missing values generated)

. 
. * Sg : 1 if avg_post > Dg1
. gen byte Sg = (avg_post > Dg1) if !missing(avg_post) & !missing(Dg1)
(1,556 missing values generated)

. 
